# The Vercel "site" project builds apps/site (which imports
# packages/patterns). Everything else in the monorepo is dead weight for
# that build — and .venv / node_modules / .build alone are ~1 GB, which
# blows past Vercel's upload limits. Keep the deploy archive lean.
#
# NOTE: archive uploads (--archive=tgz) do NOT honor .gitignore, so the
# heavy build/vendor dirs must be listed here explicitly.

.git
node_modules
**/node_modules
.turbo
**/.turbo
.next
**/.next

# Python ML-conversion venvs (torch/coreml) — hundreds of MB, desktop-only.
.venv
**/.venv
.venv-ml
**/.venv-ml

# The Swift desktop app and its build/release artifacts — not part of the site.
apps/desktop
BouclierAppIcons
*.dmg

# Generated pattern dist is rebuilt by the Vercel build command.
packages/patterns/dist
